  "name": "Authsignal",
  "abstract": "Authentication and orchestration layer from New Zealand for consumer-facing businesses. It adds FIDO-certified passkeys, step-up and adaptive MFA to an identity stack you already run, such as Amazon Cognito, Auth0, Azure AD B2C, Entra ID, Duende IdentityServer, Keycloak or WSO2, without migrating users. Authenticators include passkeys, security keys, email and SMS OTP, email magic links, authenticator apps, push and QR code verification, with WhatsApp OTP, biometrics and identity proofing on the Enterprise plan. A no-code rules engine decides when to challenge, a hosted pre-built UI or SDKs handle enrollment, and session and webhook APIs tie it to your backend. Authsignal is not an OpenID Provider. Plans start with a 30 day trial, then Professional from $0.05 per MAU per month. SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 certified.",
